 COMMENT ON FUNCTION public.dispute_tariff_compare(jsonb, jsonb) IS
-    'v5.4.2-25 (L6). rule_tables.compare_function of dispute_tariffs: against every law row in force that rules (governs law) for the utility — every class, so the most protective binds — the tariff is refused when its blocks lack one of the law''s; it admits fewer subjects; its shelter starts narrower (any_time, before_termination, before_delinquency in that order; within_days against its own kind only, the same anchor and at least the days; any other pair not comparable); its shelter ends sooner (resolution beats earlier-of-resolution-and-days; days against days; any other pair not comparable); or its must-pay asks more (undisputed_charges asks no more than any strategy, a law of full_bill or unruled is never exceeded, equal strategies compare figures — withholding by fraction, the average cap only when equal — and any other pair is not comparable). Not comparable is refused (fail toward protection). A delegation compares nothing. r2: its duties lack one of the law''s; r3: or its stages do not match the law''s — r4: the law''s stages are the tariff''s first, in order, with nothing between, each of its decider with a filing window no shorter and a decision window no longer; a stage of the tariff''s own only after the law''s last. r5: the findings and their verdicts are dispute_tariff_compare_sections''s; this returns their messages, in order. r6 (Codex B2, Opus S1; Opus N1, Fable N3): undisputed_charges withholds exactly the disputed amount, so against withhold_cap it compares as a fraction of 1 in both directions (below the law''s fraction is narrower; above it is wider), and against every other strategy asks no more; any_time admits every dispute, so it is narrower than no start, and every start is narrower than a law''s any_time.';
